From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1vivy <1vivy@tutanota.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 14:40:33 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Settings: re-home orphan-category OEM tiles to advanced
 security

OEM prebuilts com.aiunit.aon ("EZ Pay") and com.oplus.aiunit ("AI Service
Engine") declare MANUFACTURER_APPLICATION_SETTING tiles without a valid
com.android.settings.category meta-data (AON has none; AIUnit misspells it
as com.android.settings.category.export). TileUtils.loadTile() then leaves
the tile category null, tryInitCategories() stores a DashboardCategory
under a null key, and every DashboardFragment without an explicit
DashboardFragmentRegistry mapping resolves its category key to null and
renders that category, leaking both tiles into Reset options and every
other unregistered Settings subpage.

The apks are OEM-signed prebuilts, so fix it in Settings: re-home tiles
from a null/empty category key to CATEGORY_SECURITY_ADVANCED_SETTINGS and
drop the invalid key from mCategoryByKeyMap. mergeSecurityPrivacyKeys()
then migrates them to "More security and privacy" when SafetyCenter is
enabled, and they surface under "More security settings" otherwise.
---
 .../settings/dashboard/CategoryManager.java   | 40 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 40 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/com/android/settings/dashboard/CategoryManager.java b/src/com/android/settings/dashboard/CategoryManager.java
--- a/src/com/android/settings/dashboard/CategoryManager.java
+++ b/src/com/android/settings/dashboard/CategoryManager.java
@@ -161,6 +161,7 @@ public class CategoryManager {
             for (DashboardCategory category : mCategories) {
                 mCategoryByKeyMap.put(category.key, category);
             }
+            rehomeOrphanCategoryTiles(mCategoryByKeyMap);
             backwardCompatCleanupForCategory(mTileByComponentCache, mCategoryByKeyMap);
             mergeSecurityPrivacyKeys(context, mTileByComponentCache, mCategoryByKeyMap);
             sortCategories(context, mCategoryByKeyMap);
@@ -236,6 +237,45 @@ public class CategoryManager {
         }
     }
 
+    /**
+     * Re-homes tiles whose category resolved to a null or empty key into {@link
+     * CategoryKey#CATEGORY_SECURITY_ADVANCED_SETTINGS} and removes the invalid
+     * category from the key map.
+     *
+     * Some OEM prebuilts declare a MANUFACTURER_APPLICATION_SETTING tile without
+     * a valid com.android.settings.category meta-data, so TileUtils resolves
+     * their category to null. Every DashboardFragment missing an explicit
+     * DashboardFragmentRegistry mapping also looks up its tiles with a null
+     * category key, so such tiles would otherwise leak into every unregistered
+     * subpage. Tagging them as advanced security keeps them in a single sensible
+     * location and lets {@link #mergeSecurityPrivacyKeys} migrate them to
+     * "More security and privacy" when SafetyCenter is enabled.
+     */
+    @VisibleForTesting
+    synchronized void rehomeOrphanCategoryTiles(
+            Map<String, DashboardCategory> categoryByKeyMap) {
+        final List<String> orphanKeys = new ArrayList<>();
+        for (Entry<String, DashboardCategory> categoryEntry : categoryByKeyMap.entrySet()) {
+            if (TextUtils.isEmpty(categoryEntry.getKey())) {
+                orphanKeys.add(categoryEntry.getKey());
+            }
+        }
+        for (String orphanKey : orphanKeys) {
+            final DashboardCategory orphanCategory = categoryByKeyMap.remove(orphanKey);
+            final String newCategoryKey = CategoryKey.CATEGORY_SECURITY_ADVANCED_SETTINGS;
+            for (Tile tile : orphanCategory.getTiles()) {
+                tile.setCategory(newCategoryKey);
+                // move tile to new category.
+                DashboardCategory newCategory = categoryByKeyMap.get(newCategoryKey);
+                if (newCategory == null) {
+                    newCategory = new DashboardCategory(newCategoryKey);
+                    categoryByKeyMap.put(newCategoryKey, newCategory);
+                }
+                newCategory.addTile(tile);
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
     /**
      * Merges {@link CategoryKey#CATEGORY_SECURITY_ADVANCED_SETTINGS} and {@link
      * CategoryKey#CATEGORY_PRIVACY} into {@link
